# Raw and derived data is regenerable by the build scripts and can reach
# many GB once the 20 m lake is built (AGENTS.md sections 10, 48). Never commit it.
#
# ANCHORED with a leading slash on purpose. A bare "data/" matches a directory named
# data at ANY depth, and it silently excluded source from version control in two
# separate places, found independently from both sides:
#   scripts/data/          two CP-03 scripts skipped by `git add -A` with no warning
#   frontend/src/sim/data/ the entire Python->browser seam -- codec.ts, manifest.ts,
#                          source.ts and their tests -- never committed at all, where a
#                          `git clean -xdf` would have deleted them with no trace.
/data/
frontend/public/sim/
env_sim/
artifacts/schema_audit/*.csv
artifacts/schema_audit/*.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Download manifests record absolute machine-specific destinations (AGENTS.md section 5)
artifacts/download_manifests/

# Python virtual environment (CP-00); rebuilt from requirements.txt
.venv/
venv/

# Tier C DRS proxy zones are regenerable from the raw mirror and are development
# aids only (never claimable). Currently partial; regenerate with:
#   python scripts/data/derive_drs_zones.py --all
artifacts/drs_zones/
